tests/fixtures/face.matte-ref.png (33,944 bytes): the reference person matte for the Studio runner's `matte` mode
(PAR-10269). 640x1080 greyscale, three 640x360 mattes stacked top to bottom, for frames 12, 48 and 84 (1 s, 4 s, 7 s)
of tests/fixtures/face.mp4. White is the person.

It is a derivative of face.mp4, so the same licence applies: CC BY 4.0, from "head-pose-face-detection-female.mp4"
(Intel Corporation, https://github.com/intel-iot-devkit/sample-videos); see face.mp4.LICENSE.

How it was made: by a different, larger model than the one under test, so the check is not circular. MODNet
(huggingface.co/Xenova/modnet, `onnx/model.onnx`, SHA-256 07c308cf0fc7e6e8b2065a12ed7fc07e1de8febb7dc7839d7b7f15dd66584df9,
Apache-2.0) ran on each frame scaled to 896x512 (bicubic), input (x/255 - 0.5) / 0.5, and its alpha was scaled back to
640x360 (bicubic). Each matte was checked by eye against its frame (hair, shoulders, arms; no background).
